<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">Independence March</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">words adopted 12 March <a href="/years/1921">1921</a>; music adopted <a href="/years/1930">1930</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as İstiklal Marşı</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">&quot;<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/istiklal-mars">İstiklal Marşı</a>&quot; (&quot;Independence March&quot;) is the national anthem of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/republic-of-turkey">Republic of Turkey</a> and of the Turkish Republic of Northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyprus">Cyprus</a>. It was made during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkish-war-of-independence">Turkish War of Independence</a>, when the Turkish National Movement led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mustafa-kemal-ataturk">Mustafa Kemal Atatürk</a> was fighting both invading foreign powers and the Ottoman court, which it held to be complicit in the partition of the Turkish homeland after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-sevres">Treaty of Sèvres</a> of 1920.</p></div>
